#import "/_lib/0.1.1.typ": *
#show: template

#taxon[Lemma]
#title[Identity type of Dirichlet Product]

Let $(T,U,e,a,b)$ and $(T',U',e',a',b')$ be terms in the dirichlet product $(F
*_D G)(S)$ of #local("00DT")[species] $F$ and $G$.

Let $C(T,U,e) :-= F(T) xx G(U)$ be indexed by the type of
#local("00DQ")[cartesian decompositions], then
$
  ((T,U,e,a,b) =_(F *_D G) (T',U',e',a',b'))\
  ~= sum ((r,s,f): "Eq-cart-dec"((T,U,e), (T',U',e')), (("tr"_F (r,a) = a') xx ("tr"_G (s,b) = b'))\
$
#proof[

  Given $(A,B,e) : "cart-dec"(S)$, define $C(A,B,e) :-= F(A) xx G(B)$.
  We then have that
  $
  ((T,U,e,a,b) =_(F *_D G) (T',U',e',a',b'))\
  ~= sum (p : (T,U,e) =_"cart-dec"(S) (T',U',e')),"tr"_C (p,(a,b))=(a',b').
  $

  We make use of the following charcterization of the idenity type of cartesian
  decompositions constructed #local("00DY")[here], and denote it by $iota$.
  $
    iota : (sum (p: A ~= A', q : B ~= B'), e' @ (p xx q) = e)
    arrow.long^~  ((A,B,e) =_"cart-dec"(S) (A',B',e'))
  $

  With that the equivalence becomes
  $
  ((T,U,e,a,b) =_(F *_D G) (T',U',e',a',b'))\
  ~= sum ((r,s,f): "Eq-cart-dec"(S), ("tr"_C (iota(r,s,f), (a,b)) = (a',b'))\
  $
  Here we are using that, given some equivalence of types $p: A ~= A'$, we get
  an equivalence $sum (a : A), B(p(a)) ~= sum (a: A'), B(a)$.

  Now since $C(A,B,e)$ is constant in $e$ we have by #local("00EH")[this lemma], that
  $
    ("tr"_C (iota(r),(a,b))=(a',b'))\
    ~= (("tr"_F (p, a) = a') xx ("tr"_F (q, b) = b')).
  $
  
  We conclude that 
  $
  ((T,U,e,a,b) =_(F *_D G) (T',U',e',a',b'))\
  ~= sum ((r,s,f): "Eq-cart-dec"(S)), (("tr"_F (p, a) = a') xx ("tr"_F (q, b) = b'))
  $
]
